  "label": "User projected onto the visual material as the target of violence",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material (armed_individuals) as the target of the violence described in the text. The phrase 'they always blow up in your face' directly implicates the user ('your face') as the recipient of the violence, thereby projecting the user onto the scene where the armed individuals are depicted. The user is not just a passive observer but is positioned as the potential victim of the group's actions.",
